sieve-filter-v2
; melody-leap-v1 for the notes3 family: no leap between neighbouring notes wider than `leap`
; semitones, whatever their lengths and loudness. Rests are passed over, or, with rest_resets, let
; the next note be anything. The state is the last note's pitch (0: none yet).
; On a notes3 line the notes of one pitch, at every level and length, are one run of symbols,
; NOTE(p, 1, 1) to NOTE(p, LEVELS, LONGEST), and the rests another, REST(1) to REST(LONGEST).
id        melody-leap-notes3
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes3*
describe  No two neighbouring notes further apart than the leap, in semitones.
param     leap         int     4  1  24  the widest step between neighbouring notes, in semitones
param     rest_resets  choice  no no,yes whether a rest lets the next note be anything

states    {PITCHES + 1}
start     0
accept    0..{PITCHES}
t 0 @{REST(1)}..@{REST(LONGEST)} 0
for p 1 {PITCHES}
  t 0 @{NOTE(p, 1, 1)}..@{NOTE(p, LEVELS, LONGEST)} {p}
  if {rest_resets == 1}
    t {p} @{REST(1)}..@{REST(LONGEST)} 0
  else
    t {p} @{REST(1)}..@{REST(LONGEST)} {p}
  fi
  for q {max(1, p - leap)} {min(PITCHES, p + leap)}
    t {p} @{NOTE(q, 1, 1)}..@{NOTE(q, LEVELS, LONGEST)} {q}
  done
done
end
